    "created_at": "2023-03-17T03:24:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-17T03:24:16Z",
    "body": "In https://github.com/WICG/web-app-launch/issues/86 , the owner would like to support `\"launch_handler\": { \"client_mode\": \"service-worker\" }` in PWA manifest launch_handler in the future.\r\n\r\nLet me further explain why the current click behavior (navigation behavior) on custom protocol link is not ideal. Traditional web page links are used to display a content for human, but some other URI protocols are not designed for human to see. For example, [magnet link](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnet_URI_scheme) is designed for adding a download task in BitTorrent clients, it is not designed for human to see something. These links are not suitable for navigating to a register page. Instead, handling these links in the background is the best way.",
